#
# To mint a Zenodo DOI: enable this repository on Zenodo
# (https://zenodo.org), create a new GitHub release, and Zenodo will archive it
# and issue a DOI. Then add the resulting DOI to this file as a top-level
# `doi:` field and an `identifiers:` block, e.g.:
#
#   doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#       description: The concept DOI for all versions.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "The OpenBiomechanics Project (OBP)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Driveline Baseball Research and Development"
  - family-names: "Boddy"
    given-names: "Kyle"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drivelineresearch/openbiomechanics"
url: "https://openbiomechanics.org"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - biomechanics
  - baseball
  - motion capture
  - pitching
  - hitting
  - force plate
  - sports science
abstract: >-
  The OpenBiomechanics Project is a freely available library of
  research-grade biomechanics data, providing full-body marker-based motion
  capture and force plate measurements of baseball pitching and hitting to
  support open sports-science research.
